interview  requests they have to give up front a  compensation indicative compensation  information as well so it's not a thing  that they asked was so what if  candidates actually had a career  counselor / career advisor helping them  along the entire process and a lot of  times you know you you you you have  recruiters and and other people who are  very directly kind of financially  incentivized to put you into a job that  you either may or may not like so having  someone having someone who is completely  objective who's able to kind of be there  when you need them and  and and push you through the the process  of interviewing and assessing different  companies you know that of course is is  incredibly valuable for you as a  candidate and lastly what if you were  actually rewarded for getting a job I  mean it's quite an achievement you've  gone through this kind of like sometimes  a stressful exercise and you know  getting a job it's obviously like  incredibly it's an amazing feeling  you're really really excited so  shouldn't you be rewarded for that and  that's exactly what happens when you get  hired on the hired platform so if you  get hired in Singapore we actually give  you a service play one Wi-Fi speaker I  should have two at home they're amazing  so basically I just want to talk really  briefly about what a good profile looks  like when you're presenting yourself as  a software engineer to employers so in  my personal experience what I've  actually seen be really really  successful is candidate to tell a story  so you always kind of hear about like  like people in marketing and brands  being very successful about engaging  their audience and getting people  interested by telling a story a CV a  hired profile it's exactly the same  thing when you tell a story about  yourself it gets people engaged it gets  people interested so the the profiles  that really get a lot of people's  attention oh really ones that kind of  talk about you know what got you into  stuff software engineering what are you  passionate about why do you do this for  a living what what do you do in your  spare time thats thats related to what  you do at work those are  outlining those things will get you very  very far far in making yourself stand  out amongst a lot of other potential  candidates for the same role the other  thing that is incredibly important is to  really kind of flush out all the other  things that you do at outside of your  day-to-day job that could include you  know open source contribution you know  your activity on github your activity on  stack overflow and other other different  channels side projects is it something  that you should always present in terms  of you know what you're tinkering with  because it helps employers really  understand how you think and also what  you're what you're really interested in  in as well so who's hiring excuse me so  a short answer pretty much everybody so  in the context of Singapore there are so  many companies right now that are hiring  for software engineers those include  that you know obviously like the the  success stories here in Singapore you  know carousel kareena Sephora digital  but there is also a really long list of  incredible fast growing tech companies  here and there in across many many  different industries so in FinTech there  in AI there in SAS there in autonomous  cars healthcare travel there's so much  opportunities out there for software  engineers right now that it's it's it's  really up to candidates to decide what  feel that they're interested in and you  know what kind of roles and  responsibilities that they would  actually like to take on in their next  role and and also there's incredibly  large kind of public companies that are  hiring quite substantial software  engineering teams  in Singapore as well a key example you  you probably know that a lot of the big  financial services companies are  creating innovation centers and  innovation labs here in Singapore so  there's just an incredible list of of  companies who are hiring for for  engineers and it just continues to grow  and for those of you who are engineers  from outside of Singapore this and are  potentially open to relocating here  again fantastic opportunities and a lot  of the companies here in Singapore are  open to relocating candidates from  elsewhere and and the visa process here  is is very very straightforward so just  a quick overview on what we've seen at  hired so this is the average salary in  singapore by broken down by the years of  experience of software engineers with  javascript experience here in singapore  so in some markets what you'll find is  that salaries start off very high  straight out of a university or straight  out of school and then they plateau very  quickly in singapore it's a little bit  different so in singapore the salary  actually grows quite quickly as you as  you gain experience and at the very  senior levels it actually gets to quite  quite high numbers so lastly i just want  to say a quick thanks to to the sponsor  to the organizers for the jus comp this  year we are great supporters of the j s  community as well as other tech  communities at higher and we look  forward to hopefully helping many of you  folks out there at some point in the  future find your next dream job thank  you very much  you
 

